 "summary": "Commodities were broadly weaker in the latest session, with 10 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 13 lower. Energy was mixed, 2 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Coal (Newcastle) at +2.19% to 144.85 USD/T; precious metals were mixed, 4 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Rhodium at +1.10% to 9200 USD/t oz; base metals were mixed, 2 of 6 higher, the biggest move coming from Zinc at -1.34% to 3855.60 USD/T; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 2 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41% to 99.33 USD/T; agriculture fell across the board, led by Corn at -2.16% to 510.22 USd/Bu. The largest single move across the complex was Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41%. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Bitget on 01 September 2026:",
